  "contracts": {
    "world": "Persistent trusted mapped World; initialize once, never reset/reuse. Disjoint48-bit ranges are burned on reservation, including unused IDs at retirement. PAYLOAD+1 is exhausted sentinel.",
    "publication": "capacity0 refused; phase0 unpublished,1live,2retired. All initializer refusal checks precede reservation; no rollback of World. Complete Instance fields precede used increment. retire only changes phase.",
    "lookup": "Exact stored handle, owner/catalog base, entry index/target and current target table value; validates live/used/range arithmetic before entry access. Returns target+1 or0 refusal, never a guest native address.",
    "preconditions": "Descriptors/embedded pointers are trusted entry-owned metadata, not wire or guest input. Caller supplies real mapped extents, exclusive mutable storage separated from executing control/helpers, retained immutable target table, serial service calls. Arithmetic does not authenticate mappings; descriptor corruption can violate these preconditions.",
    "limits": "No cross-world authentication, handle inputs/outputs/imports, catalog/image verification, managed lifetime/GC/reclamation, borrowed physical parameter admission, guest closure execution, or active frame transition claim."
  },
